  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0274">Lemma <span data-tag="0274">110.47.1</span>.</a> There exists an affine scheme $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and an injective $A$-module $J$ such that $\widetilde{J}$ is not a flasque sheaf on $X$. Even the restriction $\Gamma (X, \widetilde{J}) \to \Gamma (U, \widetilde{J})$ with $U$ a standard open need not be surjective. </p>
